  "aiSummary": "This bill removes a specific 18.93-acre parcel of property from the corporate limits of the City of Washington in Beaufort County. After the bill takes effect on June 30, 2026, the property will no longer be subject to City of Washington municipal taxes, though any existing tax liens will still be collectible.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters may argue that deannexation allows property owners to reduce their tax burden by removing them from municipal taxation. They may contend that the property is not receiving adequate city services to justify municipal taxes, or that property owners prefer county governance and lower county tax rates.",
  "aiConArguments": "Opponents may argue that deannexation reduces the city's tax base and revenue needed to maintain municipal services for remaining residents. They may also contend that removing developed property near the airport creates an inefficient city boundary and shifts service costs to other city taxpayers.",
